{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfnHaCb5oXX4ricRXkUG5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I approved six of the seven rows and returned TC-328, so the batch outcome is `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=7`. The approval is committed and anchored.\n\n**Approved: LLR-307, LLR-308, LLR-310, SR-232, TC-325, TC-327**\n- **LLR-307:** it now matches the code. Only a row never claimed through the lane is released. An unreadable claim, an unreadable current copy, or a claimed row whose spec is gone each hold the lane and say why. Deleting a Done-when section owes a blessing.\n- **LLR-308:** it now covers the done-when brief alone, and it states the 120-line Context clip (`CANDIDATE_CLIP`).\n- **SR-232:** each hat is now argued by the failure it actually catches. UNATTENDED-OPS catches a checkpoint passing with a requested kind never judged; INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY catches one kind acting while another section refuses.\n- **LLR-310 and TC-327:** both went back last round only because their parents did; those parents are now ready.\n- **TC-325:** every claim now has a test that exercises it, including `test_a_test_run_is_never_held`, which runs pytest in a lane that is being held.\n\n**Returned: TC-328.** Its Evidence and Expected now cite the BLESSED-cover and no-draft SUCCESSOR tests. But its Method still lists only the seven older tests to run, while asking you to assert the two outcomes only the new tests produce. The fix is to add those two test names to the Method.\n\n**Separate coverage gap:** LLR-307 says a decision entry carrying the retired key doesn't release the hold. The code does this (`covering` treats such an entry as unseen), but no cited test checks it. I approved LLR-307 anyway, because the gap is in the tests rather than the text. I drafted a follow-up to add that test and cite it from TC-326. TC-326 is already approved, so citing the test there will need its own amendment adjudication.\n\n**Commits:**\n- `45602bc3` — the verdict file `007-ADJUDICATE-88314d5.md` plus a new `## Dispositions` section in the spec holding the draft above, with the trailer `WI: WI-841`.\n- `793cd196` — the approval act: the six Status flips plus the snapshot of all three registries (act ledger seq 47), also with `WI: WI-841`.\n\nThe snapshot wasn't refused, so nothing else in those registries has drifted. TC-328 stays Drafted inside the copied test-case registry. The pre-commit checks passed on both commits, and the working tree is clean."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":691,"cache_read_input_tokens":233211,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":691},"output_tokens":754,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2cffbbc6-0175-4e90-b9ab-7b165e0c0246","uuid":"e436150b-9f23-4736-833d-bcd37126694a","timestamp":"2026-10-07T04:59:38.976Z","request_id":"req_011CfnHaCHEQaCxGLCHHnj6g"}
